# Line-ending policy for every checkout of this repository.
#
# Measured problem (2026-10-18): a Windows checkout runs with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and therefore writes CRLF into the working tree, while
# the same clone used from WSL/Linux has `core.autocrlf` unset. That git then
# reported **74 tracked files as modified** even though the index was already
# all-LF; only `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` revealed that nothing but the line
# endings differed. `* text=auto` makes git normalize on the way into the index
# and on the way out to the comparison, so both sides agree on what "modified"
# means without forcing anybody's editor or checkout style.
#
# Deliberately NOT `eol=lf`: that would rewrite the 74 CRLF files a Windows
# checkout already has, turning the same phantom diff into a real one there.
* text=auto

# Never normalize binary artifacts.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.tgz binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.zst binary
*.gz binary
*.asar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
